{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "def remove_Occ(string, character):\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes the first and last occurrence of a given character from the string.\n    If the character appears only once, that single occurrence is removed.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_idx = string.find(character)\n    last_idx = string.rfind(character)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:  # Character not found\n        return string\n\n    indices_to_remove = set()\n    if first_idx == last_idx:  # Only one occurrence\n        indices_to_remove.add(first_idx)\n    else:  # Two or more occurrences\n        indices_to_remove.add(first_idx)\n        indices_to_remove.add(last_idx)\n\n    result_chars = []\n    for i, char_val in enumerate(string):\n        if i not in indices_to_remove:\n            result_chars.append(char_val)\n\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/9", "solution": "def _calculate_period(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculate the period (shortest repeating unit length) of a string.\"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    \n    # KMP LPS array construction\n    lps = [0] * n\n    length = 0  # length of the previous longest prefix suffix\n    i = 1\n    \n    while i < n:\n        if s[i] == s[length]:\n            length += 1\n            lps[i] = length\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            if length != 0:\n                length = lps[length - 1]\n            else:\n                lps[i] = 0\n                i += 1\n                \n    # The length of the smallest repeating unit (period) is derived from the LPS array.\n    # If a string 's' has length 'n' and its longest proper prefix which is also a suffix has length lps[n-1],\n    # then the potential period is n - lps[n-1].\n    # If 'n' is perfectly divisible by this potential period, then it's the actual period.\n    # Otherwise, the string cannot be formed by repeating a smaller unit, so its period is 'n'.\n    potential_period = n - lps[n-1]\n    \n    if n % potential_period == 0:\n        return potential_period\n    else:\n        return n\n\ndef find_Rotations(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find minimum number of rotations greater than 0 to restore string to original form.\n    \"\"\"\n    # For an empty string or a single-character string, one rotation (of 1 character)\n    # is the minimum greater than 0 to get the same string.\n    if len(s) <= 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # The minimum number of 1-character rotations required to get the same string\n    # is equivalent to the length of its shortest repeating unit (its period).\n    return _calculate_period(s)"}
