{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence using memoization.\n    The sequence is defined by P(1)=1, P(2)=1, and P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n-P(n-1)) for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _initialize_base_cases() -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Initializes and returns the base cases for the Newman-Conway sequence.\"\"\"\n        return {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n    memo = _initialize_base_cases()\n\n    def _calculate_newman_conway(k: int, current_memo: dict) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Recursively calculates the Newman-Conway number for a given position k,\n        using and updating the provided memoization cache.\n        \"\"\"\n        if k in current_memo:\n            return current_memo[k]\n\n        # Apply the recurrence relation: P(k) = P(P(k-1)) + P(k-P(k-1))\n        p_k_minus_1 = _calculate_newman_conway(k - 1, current_memo)\n        \n        val = _calculate_newman_conway(p_k_minus_1, current_memo) + _calculate_newman_conway(k - p_k_minus_1, current_memo)\n        current_memo[k] = val\n        return val\n\n    return _calculate_newman_conway(n, memo)"}
