{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number A(n, m) using dynamic programming.\n    This function computes the number of permutations of {1, ..., n} with exactly m ascents.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle base cases and out-of-bounds conditions for Eulerian numbers\n    if n < 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1 if m == 0 else 0\n    if m < 0 or m >= n:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize a 2D DP table: dp[i][j] will store A(i, j)\n    # The table size is (n+1) x (n+1) to accommodate indices from 0 to n for both i and j.\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: A(i, 0) = 1 for all i >= 0\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        dp[i][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table using the recurrence relation:\n    # A(i, j) = (j + 1) * A(i-1, j) + (i - j) * A(i-1, j-1)\n    # i represents the 'n' in A(n, m), and j represents the 'm' in A(n, m).\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):  # Iterate for 'n' from 1 up to the given n\n        for j in range(1, i):  # Iterate for 'm' from 1 up to n-1 (i-1)\n            dp[i][j] = (j + 1) * dp[i-1][j] + (i - j) * dp[i-1][j-1]\n\n    # The result is the value stored at dp[n][m]\n    return dp[n][m]"}
