{"task_id": "Mbpp/120", "solution": "def max_product_tuple(tuples_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum absolute product between numbers in pairs of tuples within a given list.\n    Assumes valid input where each tuple contains two numeric values.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_abs_product = 0.0\n\n    for a, b in tuples_list:\n        current_abs_product = abs(a * b)\n        if current_abs_product > max_abs_product:\n            max_abs_product = current_abs_product\n\n    return max_abs_product"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "def amicable_numbers_sum(limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all amicable numbers up to a specified limit.\n    Uses helper functions to determine proper divisor sums and amicable property.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def sum_of_proper_divisors(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of proper divisors for a given number.\"\"\"\n        if n <= 1:\n            return 0\n        s = 1  # 1 is always a proper divisor\n        for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n            if n % i == 0:\n                s += i\n                if i * i != n:\n                    s += n // i\n        return s\n\n    def is_amicable_number(n: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a number is part of an amicable pair.\"\"\"\n        if n <= 1:\n            return False\n        sum_div_n = sum_of_proper_divisors(n)\n        if sum_div_n == n or sum_div_n <= n: # Optimization: d(n) must be > n to be part of an amicable pair (excluding perfect numbers)\n            return False\n\n        sum_div_partner = sum_of_proper_divisors(sum_div_n)\n        return sum_div_partner == n\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(1, limit + 1):\n        if is_amicable_number(i):\n            total_sum += i\n    return total_sum"}
