{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "def sum_range_list(numbers: list, start_index: int, end_index: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of numbers in a list within a specified index range (inclusive).\n    Handles invalid or out-of-bounds indices gracefully by returning 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Python's list slicing naturally handles various edge cases:\n    # - Negative start_index is treated as 0.\n    # - end_index + 1 exceeding list length is treated as list length.\n    # - If the resulting slice is empty (e.g., start_index > end_index, or list is empty),\n    #   sum() applied to an empty list returns 0, which is graceful error handling.\n    sublist = numbers[start_index : end_index + 1]\n    return sum(sublist)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/172", "solution": "def count_occurance(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts non-overlapping occurrences of the substring 'std' in the given string.\n    This function performs a linear scan to find all occurrences.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    search_pattern = 'std'\n    pattern_length = len(search_pattern)\n    start_index = 0\n\n    while True:\n        # Find the next occurrence of the pattern starting from start_index\n        found_index = input_string.find(search_pattern, start_index)\n\n        if found_index != -1:\n            # If found, increment count and advance start_index past the found pattern\n            count += 1\n            start_index = found_index + pattern_length\n        else:\n            # If not found, break the loop\n            break\n\n    return count"}
