{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-positioned bits (0, 2, 4, etc.) of the input number to 1.\n    This uses a fixed mask with 1s at even positions, ORing it with the number.\n    \"\"\"\n    # A mask with all even-positioned bits set to 1.\n    # For example, 0x55 is 01010101_2. 0x5555555555555555 is for 64 bits.\n    even_bits_mask = 0x5555555555555555\n    \n    # Perform a bitwise OR operation. This sets bits to 1 where they are 0 in 'number'\n    # and 1 in 'even_bits_mask', while preserving other bits and Python's arbitrary precision.\n    return number | even_bits_mask"}
