{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(arr: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence in the given array.\n    A sequence is bitonic if it is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    # Calculate LIS Sums (Longest Increasing Subsequence Sums)\n    # lis_sums[i] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at index i.\n    lis_sums = list(arr)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lis_sums[i] = max(lis_sums[i], lis_sums[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Calculate LDS Sums (Longest Decreasing Subsequence Sums)\n    # lds_sums[i] stores the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at index i.\n    lds_sums = list(arr)\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lds_sums[i] = max(lds_sums[i], lds_sums[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Combine LIS and LDS sums to find the maximum bitonic sum.\n    # For each element arr[i], it can serve as the peak of a bitonic subsequence.\n    # The sum of such a subsequence would be lis_sums[i] + lds_sums[i] - arr[i]\n    # (arr[i] is counted twice, once in LIS and once in LDS, so subtract it).\n    max_bitonic_sum = float('-inf')\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_bitonic_sum = lis_sums[i] + lds_sums[i] - arr[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    # The problem context implies integer return type from the example.\n    return int(max_bitonic_sum)"}
