{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "def max_aggregate(tuple_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate maximum aggregate from list of tuples.\n    Groups tuples by name, sums their values, and returns the name with the highest total.\n    \"\"\"\n    aggregates = {}\n    for name, value in tuple_list:\n        aggregates[name] = aggregates.get(name, 0) + value\n\n    if not aggregates:\n        return None  # Or a default empty tuple, depending on desired behavior for empty input\n\n    max_name = None\n    max_sum = float('-inf')\n\n    for name, total_sum in aggregates.items():\n        if total_sum > max_sum:\n            max_sum = total_sum\n            max_name = name\n\n    return (max_name, max_sum)"}
