{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "def large_product(list1, list2, count):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the specified number of largest products from two lists, selecting one factor from each.\n    Calculates all possible cross-products, sorts them in descending order, and returns the top 'count'.\n    \"\"\"\n    all_products = []\n    for factor1 in list1:\n        for factor2 in list2:\n            all_products.append(factor1 * factor2)\n\n    # Sort the products in descending order\n    all_products.sort(reverse=True)\n\n    # Return the top 'count' products\n    return all_products[:count]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(array, n, i, k):\n    # dp[j] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at index j (for 0 <= j <= i).\n    # Initialize dp array for the prefix up to index i.\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n    \n    # Calculate dp values for the prefix array[0...i].\n    for current_idx in range(i + 1):\n        # Base case: A subsequence ending at current_idx can just be array[current_idx] itself.\n        dp[current_idx] = array[current_idx]\n        for prev_idx in range(current_idx):\n            # If array[current_idx] can extend an increasing subsequence ending at prev_idx,\n            # update dp[current_idx] with the maximum possible sum.\n            if array[current_idx] > array[prev_idx]:\n                dp[current_idx] = max(dp[current_idx], dp[prev_idx] + array[current_idx])\n                \n    # Retrieve the value of the mandatory kth element.\n    k_value = array[k]\n    \n    # Find the maximum sum from a prefix increasing subsequence (ending at some j <= i)\n    # such that array[j] is less than k_value, allowing k_value to extend it.\n    max_sum_from_prefix_before_k = 0\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        # Only consider dp[j] if array[j] can be strictly followed by k_value.\n        if array[j] < k_value:\n            max_sum_from_prefix_before_k = max(max_sum_from_prefix_before_k, dp[j])\n            \n    # The total maximum sum is the best prefix sum found + the k_value itself.\n    # If no suitable prefix subsequence was found (max_sum_from_prefix_before_k remains 0),\n    # it implies the increasing subsequence involving array[k] is just array[k] itself.\n    return max_sum_from_prefix_before_k + k_value"}
