{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "def get_max_sum(n: int, memo: dict = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum using the equation f(n) = max((f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n),\n    with memoization for efficient computation.\n    \"\"\"\n    if memo is None:\n        memo = {}\n\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 0\n\n    if n in memo:\n        return memo[n]\n\n    # Calculate the sum of recursive calls for n/2, n/3, n/4, n/5 using integer division.\n    sum_of_children = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2, memo) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3, memo) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4, memo) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5, memo)\n    )\n\n    # The result is the maximum of the sum of children or n itself.\n    result = max(sum_of_children, n)\n    memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
