{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(array: list) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Find pair with highest product from array of integers.\n    This function generates all possible pairs and identifies the one with the maximum product.\"\"\"\n\n    def _generate_pairs(arr: list) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Generates all unique pairs from the input array.\"\"\"\n        pairs = []\n        n = len(arr)\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                pairs.append((arr[i], arr[j]))\n        return pairs\n\n    def _calculate_product(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the product of two integers.\"\"\"\n        return a * b\n\n    def _find_max_product_pair(pairs_list: list) -> tuple:\n        \"\"\"Finds the pair with the maximum product from a list of pairs.\"\"\"\n        if not pairs_list:\n            return None\n\n        max_prod = -float('inf')\n        max_pair = None\n\n        for p1, p2 in pairs_list:\n            current_prod = _calculate_product(p1, p2)\n            if current_prod > max_prod:\n                max_prod = current_prod\n                max_pair = (p1, p2)\n        return max_pair\n\n    if len(array) < 2:\n        # If the array has fewer than two elements, no pair can be formed.\n        return None\n\n    all_pairs = _generate_pairs(array)\n    result_pair = _find_max_product_pair(all_pairs)\n    return result_pair"}
