{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum product of a contiguous subarray within the given array.\n    This algorithm efficiently handles positive, negative, and zero numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Initialize variables to track the maximum product found overall,\n    # and the maximum and minimum products ending at the current position.\n    max_so_far = arr[0]\n    min_ending_here = arr[0]\n    max_ending_here = arr[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        num = arr[i]\n        \n        # Store the current max_ending_here before it gets updated.\n        # This is crucial because min_ending_here update also depends on the previous max_ending_here.\n        temp_max_ending_here = max_ending_here\n        \n        # The new maximum product ending at the current position can be the number itself,\n        # or the number multiplied by the previous max_ending_here,\n        # or the number multiplied by the previous min_ending_here (if it's a negative number).\n        max_ending_here = max(num, temp_max_ending_here * num, min_ending_here * num)\n        \n        # Similarly, the new minimum product ending at the current position.\n        min_ending_here = min(num, temp_max_ending_here * num, min_ending_here * num)\n        \n        # Update the overall maximum product found so far.\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, max_ending_here)\n\n    return max_so_far"}
