{"task_id": "Mbpp/563", "solution": "def extract_values(input_string: str) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Extract all values enclosed in double quotation marks from input string.\"\"\"\n\n    def _find_quoted_content(text: str) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Locate all quoted substrings in input text, returning content start/end indices.\"\"\"\n        quote_positions = []\n        i = 0\n        while i < len(text):\n            start_quote_idx = text.find('\"', i)\n            if start_quote_idx == -1:\n                break\n\n            end_quote_idx = text.find('\"', start_quote_idx + 1)\n            if end_quote_idx == -1:\n                break\n\n            quote_positions.append((start_quote_idx + 1, end_quote_idx))\n            i = end_quote_idx + 1\n        return quote_positions\n\n    def _extract_between_quotes(text: str, start: int, end: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Extract content between specified start and end positions.\"\"\"\n        return text[start:end]\n\n    extracted_list = []\n    quote_ranges = _find_quoted_content(input_string)\n    for start, end in quote_ranges:\n        extracted_list.append(_extract_between_quotes(input_string, start, end))\n    return extracted_list"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/564", "solution": "def count_Pairs(input_list: list[int], length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of possible unordered pairs from a list where both elements are unequal.\n    Pairs are considered based on their distinct positions in the input list.\n    \"\"\"\n    unequal_pairs_count = 0\n    # Iterate through all possible unique pairs of indices (i, j) where i < j\n    for i in range(length):\n        for j in range(i + 1, length):\n            # If the elements at these indices are not equal, increment the count\n            if input_list[i] != input_list[j]:\n                unequal_pairs_count += 1\n    return unequal_pairs_count"}
