{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "def get_ludic(limit: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates all lucid numbers up to a given limit using a sieve-like algorithm.\n    Returns an ordered list of lucid numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if limit < 1:\n        return []\n\n    ludic_numbers = []\n    # Initialize candidates with natural numbers starting from 1 up to the limit.\n    candidates = list(range(1, limit + 1))\n\n    while candidates:\n        # The first number in the current list of candidates is the next lucid number.\n        p = candidates.pop(0)\n        ludic_numbers.append(p)\n\n        # For the number 1, there is no elimination step for other numbers based on its value.\n        # The sieve elimination process effectively starts with the second lucid number (which is 2).\n        if p == 1:\n            continue\n\n        # Create a new list for the next set of candidates.\n        # Elements are kept if their 1-based position in the *current* `candidates` list\n        # is not a multiple of `p`.\n        next_candidates = []\n        count = 0\n        for val in candidates:\n            count += 1\n            if count % p != 0:\n                next_candidates.append(val)\n        \n        candidates = next_candidates\n        \n    return ludic_numbers"}
