{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "def bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number using dynamic programming based on Bell's triangle.\n    The Bell number B_n represents the number of partitions of a set of n elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a 2D array (triangle) to store Bell numbers and intermediate values.\n    # The size needs to be (n+1) x (n+1) to accommodate values up to n.\n    bell_triangle = [[0 for _ in range(n + 1)] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: The 0th Bell number is 1.\n    bell_triangle[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the triangle row by row to compute Bell numbers up to n.\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # The first element of row 'i' is the last element of the previous row 'i-1'.\n        bell_triangle[i][0] = bell_triangle[i-1][i-1]\n        # Fill the rest of the elements in the current row using the recurrence relation.\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            bell_triangle[i][j] = bell_triangle[i-1][j-1] + bell_triangle[i][j-1]\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row in Bell's triangle.\n    return bell_triangle[n][0]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/610", "solution": "def _validate_index(input_list: list, k: int):\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates that the given zero-based index k is within the bounds of the input list.\n    Raises an IndexError if the index is out of range.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not (0 <= k < len(input_list)):\n        raise IndexError(\"Index out of range\")\n\ndef _create_filtered_list(input_list: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Creates a new list by removing the element at the specified zero-based index k.\n    The original list remains unmodified.\n    \"\"\"\n    return input_list[:k] + input_list[k+1:]\n\ndef remove_kth_element(input_list: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a new list with the k'th element (1-indexed position) removed from the input_list.\n    Raises IndexError if the k'th element is out of the valid range.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Convert the 1-based k to a 0-based index for internal processing.\n    zero_based_k = k - 1\n    \n    _validate_index(input_list, zero_based_k)\n    \n    return _create_filtered_list(input_list, zero_based_k)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/611", "solution": "def max_of_nth(matrix, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum value in the specified column `n` of the input matrix.\n    It iterates through each row to compare values at column `n`.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_val = float('-inf')\n\n    for row in matrix:\n        column_value = row[n]\n        if column_value > max_val:\n            max_val = column_value\n\n    return max_val"}
