{"task_id": "Mbpp/626", "solution": "def triangle_area(radius: float) -> float | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the area of the largest triangle inscribed in a semicircle.\n    The largest triangle in a semicircle has its base as the diameter and height as the radius.\n    \"\"\"\n    if radius < 0:\n        return None\n    \n    # For the largest triangle inscribed in a semicircle,\n    # the base is the diameter (2 * radius) and the height is the radius.\n    # Area = 0.5 * base * height\n    # Area = 0.5 * (2 * radius) * radius\n    # Area = radius * radius\n    # Area = radius^2\n    return radius * radius"}
