{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "def wind_chill(wind_velocity: float, temperature: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the wind chill index given wind velocity in km/h and temperature in Celsius,\n    rounded to the nearest integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Apply the standard wind chill formula (Canadian / US variant for Celsius and km/h).\n    # This formula is often defined for temperatures <= 10\u00b0C, but is applied directly as per problem context.\n    \n    # Calculate wind velocity raised to the power of 0.16\n    v_power_0_16 = wind_velocity ** 0.16\n\n    # Compute the wind chill index using the formula\n    wind_chill_float = (\n        13.12\n        + (0.6215 * temperature)\n        - (11.37 * v_power_0_16)\n        + (0.3965 * temperature * v_power_0_16)\n    )\n\n    # Round the calculated value to the nearest integer.\n    return round(wind_chill_float)"}
