{"task_id": "Mbpp/725", "solution": "def extract_quotation(input_string: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts values enclosed within double quotation marks from the given string.\n    Processes the string in a single pass to achieve O(n) time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    extracted_values = []\n    in_quote = False\n    start_index = -1\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(input_string):\n        if char == '\"':\n            if not in_quote:\n                # Found an opening quote\n                in_quote = True\n                start_index = i + 1\n            else:\n                # Found a closing quote\n                in_quote = False\n                if start_index != -1: # Ensure a valid opening quote was found\n                    extracted_values.append(input_string[start_index:i])\n                start_index = -1 # Reset start index\n\n    return extracted_values"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/726", "solution": "def multiply_elements(input_tuple: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the product of consecutive elements in a tuple of numbers.\n    The function iterates through the input tuple, multiplying each element by the one immediately following it.\n    \"\"\"\n    products = []\n    for i in range(len(input_tuple) - 1):\n        products.append(input_tuple[i] * input_tuple[i+1])\n    return tuple(products)"}
