{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, rotation_count: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items.\n    Returns a new list without modifying the original.\n    \"\"\"\n    list_length = len(input_list)\n\n    if list_length == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Calculate the effective rotation count using modulo to handle rotations\n    # larger than the list length or negative numbers.\n    effective_rotation = rotation_count % list_length\n\n    if effective_rotation == 0:\n        return input_list[:] # Return a shallow copy if no actual rotation is needed\n\n    # Split the list into two parts: the last 'effective_rotation' elements\n    # and the remaining elements, then concatenate them in the new order.\n    rotated_part = input_list[list_length - effective_rotation:]\n    remaining_part = input_list[:list_length - effective_rotation]\n\n    return rotated_part + remaining_part"}
