{"task_id": "Mbpp/765", "solution": "def is_polite(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the nth polite number. A polite number is a positive integer that is not a power of two.\n    \"\"\"\n    polite_count = 0\n    current_num = 1\n    while True:\n        # Check if current_num is a power of 2. A positive integer x is a power of 2 if x > 0 and (x & (x - 1)) == 0.\n        is_power_of_two = (current_num > 0) and ((current_num & (current_num - 1)) == 0)\n\n        if not is_power_of_two:\n            polite_count += 1\n            if polite_count == n:\n                return current_num\n        current_num += 1"}
